        ideal: "<p>Mobile emulation profiles set <code>hasTouch: true</code>, and touch-only controls may listen for <code>touchstart</code>/<code>touchend</code> rather than a mouse <code>click</code>. Use <code>locator.tap()</code> â€” which dispatches real touch events â€” instead of <code>.click()</code>, and confirm the emulated context truly has <code>hasTouch</code> enabled (<code>tap()</code> throws if it doesn't).</p>",
